course: dictionary
lesson: 15066
title: Rewind
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: To rewind means to make something go back to an earlier point. When you rewind a video, the picture runs backwards until you reach the part you want to see again. «I missed the goal, so I will rewind the video.» Here rewind means going back to see the goal again, not going forward.
explain: Context helps you check your meaning. In «She hit rewind and watched the scene twice», the words hit and watched tell you it is about a screen or a tape. Try swapping in "go back" to see if the sentence still makes sense: "She hit go back and watched the scene twice" works, so your meaning is right.
explain: You can also rewind a story or a talk. «Let's rewind to last Tuesday and see what happened» means the speaker jumps back to an earlier time, like a flashback in a book. Rewind is a verb (rewind, rewinds, rewound, rewinding), and it can also be a noun, meaning the act of going back or the button that does it.
fact: Rewind means to make something go back to an earlier point.
fact: The past tense of rewind is «rewound», as in «She rewound the tape».
fact: Old cassette tapes and videotapes had to be rewound before you could watch them again.
fact: In a story or a talk, «let's rewind» means let's go back to an earlier point.
fact: As a noun, a rewind is the act of going back, or the button you press to go back.
exercise: «I want to see that goal again, so I will rewind the video.» What does rewind mean here? | Turn the volume up | Speed up to the very end | Stop the video for ever | *Go back to an earlier point
exercise: Yesterday Sam ___ the tape before he went out. Which word fills the gap? | rewinds | rewind | *rewound | rewinding
exercise: «Let's rewind to the start of the story and check the clues.» What does rewind mean in this sentence? | Make the story end faster | Stop reading and go to sleep | *Go back to an earlier part | Write a brand new story
test: «Let's rewind and talk about what you said at the start.» What is the speaker asking for? | A longer break | A new topic with no link to before | A faster talk | *Going back to an earlier point in the talk
test: Which phrase means the same as «rewind the video»? | Make the video longer | *Wind the video back to an earlier point | Upload the video to the internet | Delete the video for ever
exam: Mia's tape finished at the end, so she had to ___ it before she could watch the first scene again. Which word fits best? | *rewind | rewound | rewinds | rewinding
